      "post": {
        "summary": "Create category",
        "responses": {},
        "tags": [
          "Categories"
        ],
        "security": [
          {
            "BearerAuth": []
          }
        ],
        "description": "## Get Category by ID\n\nRetrieves a single category resource identified by its unique ID.\n\n### Endpoint\n\n`GET {{base_url}}/categories/{id}`\n\n**Path Parameter:**  \n| Parameter | Type | Description |  \n|-----------|------|-------------|  \n| `id` | integer | The unique identifier of the category to retrieve. In this request, `1` is used as the category ID. |\n\n### Authentication\n\nThis endpoint requires a **Bearer Token**. The token must be included in the `Authorization` header:\n\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer {{token}}\n\n ```\n\n### Request Headers\n\n| Key | Value | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Specifies that the response should be returned in JSON format. |\n\n### Expected Response\n\n**Status:** `200 OK`\n\nReturns a category object with fields such as:\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"Category Name\",\n  \"is_active\": true,\n  ...\n}\n\n ```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | integer | Unique identifier of the category. |\n| `name` | string | Name of the category. |\n| `is_active` | boolean | Indicates whether the category is currently active. |",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "is_active": {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "name": "Frozen Food",
                "is_active": true
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
